  "releaseNotes": "Version 26.6.0\n- Fast Web View: documents saved linearized (PdfDocument.Linearize).\n- Web fonts that load after the page has loaded are waited for (WaitForWebFonts).\n- Right-to-left pages (Arabic, Hebrew, Persian) are printed in place at any WebPageWidth.\n- A page that calls window.print() while it loads converts normally.\n- A page with smooth scrolling prints its sticky header at the top of the page.\n- .NET Framework projects with packages.config (Web Forms, MVC 5) get the Chromium engine in bin.\n- Header and footer settings that were ignored now apply (PdfPage.DisplayHeader, DisplayFooter, Transparency); more image formats in PdfImageSection.\n- Indic and Thai text in PdfTextSection shaped more accurately.\n- PdfDocument.Append reads damaged PDF files and keeps page labels.\n- .NET 11 supported.\n- Behavior change: appended pages no longer show the document's header and footer.\n- Full release notes: https://selectpdf.com/html-to-pdf/docs/html/Release-Notes.htm",
  "requireLicenseAcceptance": false,
  "summary": "Free, cross-platform HTML to PDF converter for .NET (Community Edition, up to 5 pages).",
